DISCLOSURES (honesty covenant #9 — no silent drift)
  • project.yml: added one additive source path `TeslaSync/shared-surfaces` to the TeslaSync (iOS) and
    TeslaSync-macOS targets — the irreducible wiring for a NEW surface directory to ship + be enumerated
    (mirrors how feature-views/dashboard-widgets are wired). No other surface's code is touched.
  • .swiftlint.yml: added `TeslaSync/shared-surfaces` to `included` so the project's lint gate covers the
    new directory. Additive; lints clean today.
  • Date: the web renders the raw ISO `release.date`; the native peer formats the SAME datum with the device
    locale's medium date style (idiomatic, as the AiUsageCard peer localizes numbers), with a raw-string
    fallback when the value is not a YYYY-MM-DD calendar date. Unit-asserted (en_US → "Mar 29, 2026").
  • Change-type category is spoken via VoiceOver (changelog.changeType.* keys); the web conveys it by dot
    colour ALONE. This is an accessibility enhancement, not a parity regression.

